{"title": "Sectional Mock #23 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>Find the number of prime numbers between 60 and 90.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>60 &#2324;&#2352; 90 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["7", "8", "6", "9"], "options_hi": ["7", "8", "6", "9"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>The prime numbers between 60 and 90 = 61, 67, 71, 73, 79, 83, 89 </p><p>Hence, the required number = 7</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The prime numbers between 60 and 90 = 61, 67, 71, 73, 79, 83, 89 </p><p>Hence, the required number = 7</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Adarsh travels 3/8 part of the journey at the speed of 27 km/h, 1/6 part of the journey at the speed of 30 km/h and rest of the journey at the speed of 33 km/h. Find the average speed of Adarsh.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2310;&#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; 3/8 &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; 27 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375;, 1/6 &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; 30 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; 33 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2310;&#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["32 km/h", "31.5 km/h", "27 km/h", "30 km/h"], "options_hi": ["32 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "31.5 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "27 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "30 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let total distance travelled by Adarsh = 24a (LCM of 8 and 6)</p><p>Remaining journey = 1  -  3/8  -  1/6 = 11/24</p><p>Total time taken = (24a*3/8)/27 + (24a*1/6)/30 + (24a*11/24)/33</p><p>= a/3 + 2a/15 + a/3</p><p>= 4a/5</p><p>Average speed = 24a/(4a/5) = 30 km/h</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let total distance travelled by Adarsh = 24a (LCM of 8 and 6)</p><p>Remaining journey = 1  -  3/8  -  1/6 = 11/24</p><p>Total time taken = (24a*3/8)/27 + (24a*1/6)/30 + (24a*11/24)/33</p><p>= a/3 + 2a/15 + a/3</p><p>= 4a/5</p><p>Average speed = 24a/(4a/5) = 30 km/h</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two hemispheres of radius 14 cm and 7 cm are melted to form a cuboidal box of length and breadth 49 cm and 12 cm respectively. Find the height of the cuboid.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>14 cm &#2324;&#2352; 7 cm &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2367;&#2328;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 49 cm &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; 12 cm &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["11 cm", "7 cm", "22 cm", "15 cm"], "options_hi": ["11 cm", "7 cm", "22 cm", "15 cm"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Volume of the hemispheres = Volume of the cuboid</p><p>2/3 * 22/7 * (14<sup>3</sup> + 7<sup>3</sup>) = 49*12*h</p><p>6468 = 49*12*h</p><p>h = 11 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Volume of the hemispheres = Volume of the cuboid</p><p>2/3 * 22/7 * (14<sup>3</sup> + 7<sup>3</sup>) = 49*12*h</p><p>6468 = 49*12*h</p><p>h = 11 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>If expression (x<sup>2</sup> + Px  -  44) is completely divisible by (x + 11) and (x  -  Q), then what is the value of Q?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2309;&#2349;&#2367;&#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; (x<sup>2</sup> + Px - 44) &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; (x + 11) &#2324;&#2352; (x - Q) &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; Q &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["7", "6", "5", "4"], "options_hi": ["7", "6", "5", "4"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Since, f(x) = (x<sup>2</sup> + Px  -  44) is divisible by (x + 11).</p><p>f(-11) = 0</p><p>(-11)<sup>2</sup> + P(-11)  -  44 = 0</p><p>121  -  11P  -  44 = 0</p><p>77 = 11P</p><p>P = 7</p><p>(x<sup>2</sup> + Px  -  44) = (x<sup>2</sup> + 7x  -  44)</p><p>(x<sup>2</sup> + 11x  -  4x  -  44)</p><p>x(x + 11)  -  4(x + 11)</p><p>(x + 11)(x  -  4) is divisible by (x + 11) and (x  -  Q).</p><p>Hence, the value of Q is 4.</p><p><b> Alternate solution</b></p><p>-11*Q = -44(product of the roots of the equation)</p><p>Therefore Q =4</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Since, f(x) = (x<sup>2</sup> + Px  -  44) is divisible by (x + 11).</p><p>f(-11) = 0</p><p>(-11)<sup>2</sup> + P(-11)  -  44 = 0</p><p>121  -  11P  -  44 = 0</p><p>77 = 11P</p><p>P = 7</p><p>(x<sup>2</sup> + Px  -  44) = (x<sup>2</sup> + 7x  -  44)</p><p>(x<sup>2</sup> + 11x  -  4x  -  44)</p><p>x(x + 11)  -  4(x + 11)</p><p>(x + 11)(x  -  4) is divisible by (x + 11) and (x  -  Q).</p><p>Hence, the value of Q is 4.</p><p><b> Alternate solution</b></p><p>-11*Q = -44(product of the roots of the equation)</p><p>Therefore Q =4</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>An inlet pipe A can fill a tank in 24 minutes whereas outlet pipe B takes 40 minutes to empty the tank, then find the time taken by both pipes together to fill the tank completely.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2311;&#2344;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; 24 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2310;&#2313;&#2335;&#2354;&#2375;&#2335; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; B &#2325;&#2379; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 40 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346;&#2379;&#2306; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["50 minutes", "64 minutes", "75 minutes", "60 minutes"], "options_hi": ["50 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "64 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "75 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "60 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Total capacity = LCM of 24 and 40 = 120 units</p><p>Part filled by pipe A = 120/24 = 5 units/minute</p><p>Part emptied by pipe B = 120/40 = 3 units/minute</p><p>Time taken by both pipes together to fill the tank = 120/(5  -  3) = 60 minutes</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total capacity = LCM of 24 and 40 = 120 units</p><p>Part filled by pipe A = 120/24 = 5 units/minute</p><p>Part emptied by pipe B = 120/40 = 3 units/minute</p><p>Time taken by both pipes together to fill the tank = 120/(5  -  3) = 60 minutes</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>A merchant bought two articles for Rs. 8500 each. He sold one article at a loss of 12%. At what price (in Rs.) should he sell the other article to earn a profit of 16% overall?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2344;&#2375; 8500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2319;&#2305; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2368;&#2306;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; 12% &#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366;&#2404; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; 16% &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; (&#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 12240", "Rs. 12440", "Rs. 12340", "Rs. 12540"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 12240", "&#2352;&#2369;. 12440", "&#2352;&#2369;. 12340", "&#2352;&#2369;. 12540"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>S.P of 1<sup>st</sup> article = 8500 * 88/100 = Rs. 7480 </p><p>S.P of both articles = (8500 * 2) * 116/100 = Rs. 19720 </p><p>S.P of 2<sup>nd</sup> article = 19720  -  7480 = Rs. 12240 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>S.P of 1<sup>st</sup> article = 8500 * 88/100 = Rs. 7480 </p><p>S.P of both articles = (8500 * 2) * 116/100 = Rs. 19720 </p><p>S.P of 2<sup>nd</sup> article = 19720  -  7480 = Rs. 12240 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>Simplify:</p><p><div>&nbsp;(&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">7", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2352;&#2354;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;:</p><p><div>&nbsp;(&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">7", "options_en": ["16(3/8)", "17(1/4)", "15(5/8)", "12(1/2)"], "options_hi": ["16(3/8)", "17(1/4)", "15(5/8)", "12(1/2)"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=184 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20562/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=128 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20562/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=95 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20562/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=91 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20562/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=68 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20562/image006.png\"></p><p><img width=67 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20562/image007.png\"></p><p><img width=47 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20562/image008.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=184 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20562/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=128 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20562/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=95 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20562/image004.png\"></p><p><img width=91 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20562/image005.png\"></p><p><img width=68 height=36 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20562/image006.png\"></p><p><img width=67 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20562/image007.png\"></p><p><img width=47 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p20562/image008.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If X<sup>2</sup> + 81Y<sup>2</sup> + 2X + 1 = 0, then find the value of X<sup>84 </sup>+ Y<sup>76</sup>. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; X<sup>2</sup> + 81Y<sup>2</sup> + 2X + 1 = 0, &#2340;&#2379; X<sup>84</sup>+ Y<sup>76</sup> &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["-1", "1", "0", "-2"], "options_hi": ["-1", "1", "0", "-2"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>X<sup>2</sup> + 81Y<sup>2</sup> + 2X + 1 = 0</p><p>(X<sup>2</sup> + 2X + 1) + 81Y<sup>2</sup> = 0 </p><p>(X + 1)<sup>2</sup> + 81Y<sup>2</sup> = 0 </p><p>Since (X + 1)<sup>2</sup> &ge; 0 and 81Y<sup>2</sup> &ge; 0 </p><p>(X + 1)<sup>2</sup> = 0 </p><p>X = -1 </p><p>81Y<sup>2</sup> = 0 </p><p>Y = 0 </p><p>Hence, X<sup>84</sup> + Y<sup>76</sup> = 1 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>X<sup>2</sup> + 81Y<sup>2</sup> + 2X + 1 = 0</p><p>(X<sup>2</sup> + 2X + 1) + 81Y<sup>2</sup> = 0 </p><p>(X + 1)<sup>2</sup> + 81Y<sup>2</sup> = 0 </p><p>Since (X + 1)<sup>2</sup> &ge; 0 and 81Y<sup>2</sup> &ge; 0 </p><p>(X + 1)<sup>2</sup> = 0 </p><p>X = -1 </p><p>81Y<sup>2</sup> = 0 </p><p>Y = 0 </p><p>Hence, X<sup>84</sup> + Y<sup>76</sup> = 1 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Average of set of five numbers (including 'a') is 19.4 and average of 'b', 'c' and 'd' is 15. If average of 'a', 'b', 'c' and 'd' is 15.5, then find the new average of the set (excluding 'a').</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2305;&#2330; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; ('a' &#2360;&#2361;&#2367;&#2340;) &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; 19.4 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 'b', 'c' &#2324;&#2352; 'd' &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; 15 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 'a', 'b', 'c' &#2324;&#2352; 'd' &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376; 15.5 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; ('a' &#2325;&#2379; &#2331;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2352;) &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["18", "16", "24", "20"], "options_hi": ["18", "16", "24", "20"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Sum of 5 numbers including 'a' = 5 * 19.4 = 97</p><p>Sum of 'b', 'c' and 'd' = 3 * 15 = 45</p><p>Sum of 'a', 'b', 'c' and 'd' = 4 * 15.5 = 62</p><p>Value of 'a' = 62  -  45 = 17</p><p>Sum of 4 numbers when 'a' is excluded = 97  -  17 = 80</p><p>Required average = 80/4</p><p>= 20</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Sum of 5 numbers including 'a' = 5 * 19.4 = 97</p><p>Sum of 'b', 'c' and 'd' = 3 * 15 = 45</p><p>Sum of 'a', 'b', 'c' and 'd' = 4 * 15.5 = 62</p><p>Value of 'a' = 62  -  45 = 17</p><p>Sum of 4 numbers when 'a' is excluded = 97  -  17 = 80</p><p>Required average = 80/4</p><p>= 20</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>The angle of elevation of a ladder against a wall is 45&deg;. The length of the ladder is 12 m. what is the distance between the wall and the foot of the ladder?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2335;&#2367;&#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2368;&#2338;&#2364;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; 45&deg; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2368;&#2338;&#2364;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 12m &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2342;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2368;&#2338;&#2364;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["3&radic;2 m", "5&radic;3 m", "4&radic;3 m", "6&radic;2 m"], "options_hi": ["3&radic;2 m", "5&radic;3 m", "4&radic;3 m", "6&radic;2 m"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img border=0 width=197 height=186 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21831/image036.jpg\"></p><p>Sin 45&deg; = AB/BC</p><p>=&gt; 1/&radic;2 = AB/12</p><p>=&gt; AB = 12/&radic;2</p><p>=&gt; AB = 6&radic;2 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img border=0 width=197 height=186 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21831/image036.jpg\"></p><p>Sin 45&deg; = AB/BC</p><p>=&gt; 1/&radic;2 = AB/12</p><p>=&gt; AB = 12/&radic;2</p><p>=&gt; AB = 6&radic;2 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Height & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the largest number which divides 258, 314, and 356 and leaves same remainder in each case.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2357;&#2361; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2379; 258, 314 &#2324;&#2352; 356 &#2325;&#2379; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2331;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["21", "14", "18", "24"], "options_hi": ["21", "14", "18", "24"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Required number = HCF of (356  -  314), (356  -  258) and (314  -  258)</p><p>= HCF of (42, 98, 56)</p><p>42 = 7 * 3 * 2</p><p>98 = 2 * 7 * 7</p><p>56 = 7 * 2 * 2 * 2</p><p>HCF = 7 * 2 = 14</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Required number = HCF of (356  -  314), (356  -  258) and (314  -  258)</p><p>= HCF of (42, 98, 56)</p><p>42 = 7 * 3 * 2</p><p>98 = 2 * 7 * 7</p><p>56 = 7 * 2 * 2 * 2</p><p>HCF = 7 * 2 = 14</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find x if:</p><p><img width=151 height=87 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image165.gif\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367;</p><p><img width=\"151\" height=\"87\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image165.gif\"> &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; x &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["2", "1", "0", "-1"], "options_hi": ["2", "1", "0", "-1"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Given,</p><p><img width=156 height=87 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image166.gif\"></p><p><img width=153 height=97 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image167.gif\"></p><p><img width=191 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image168.gif\"></p><p><img width=55 height=24 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image169.gif\"></p><p>Hence the value of x is 1.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given,</p><p><img width=156 height=87 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image166.gif\"></p><p><img width=153 height=97 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image167.gif\"></p><p><img width=191 height=71 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image168.gif\"></p><p><img width=55 height=24 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p13744/image169.gif\"></p><p>Hence the value of x is 1.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 7cos x - sec x = 4&radic;3 . cos x, then find the value of (cos<sup>2</sup> x  -  7).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 7cos x - sec x = 4&radic;3 . cos x &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (cos<sup>2</sup> x - 7) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["2&radic;3", "&radic;3", "8&radic;3", "4&radic;3"], "options_hi": ["2&radic;3", "&radic;3", "8&radic;3", "4&radic;3"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>7cos x - sec x = 4&radic;3 . cos x</p><p>=&gt; 7cos<sup>2</sup> x - 1 = 4&radic;3 cos<sup>2</sup> x</p><p>=&gt; (7  -  4&radic;3) cos<sup>2</sup> x = 1</p><p>=&gt; cos<sup>2</sup> x = 1/(7  -  4&radic;3) * (7 + 4&radic;3)/(7 + 4&radic;3)</p><p>=&gt; cos<sup>2</sup> x = 7 + 4&radic;3</p><p>=&gt; (cos<sup>2</sup> x  -  7) = 4&radic;3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>7cos x - sec x = 4&radic;3 . cos x</p><p>=&gt; 7cos<sup>2</sup> x - 1 = 4&radic;3 cos<sup>2</sup> x</p><p>=&gt; (7  -  4&radic;3) cos<sup>2</sup> x = 1</p><p>=&gt; cos<sup>2</sup> x = 1/(7  -  4&radic;3) * (7 + 4&radic;3)/(7 + 4&radic;3)</p><p>=&gt; cos<sup>2</sup> x = 7 + 4&radic;3</p><p>=&gt; (cos<sup>2</sup> x  -  7) = 4&radic;3</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>14700 students appeared in an exam. 45% of the boys and 80% of the girls cleared the examination. If the total percentage of students qualifying is 65%, how many boys appeared in the exam? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>14700 &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319;&#2404; 45% &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 80% &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2347;&#2354; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; 65% &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["8400", "4200", "6300", "2100"], "options_hi": ["8400", "4200", "6300", "2100"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=310 height=106 id=\"Picture 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27135/image003.png\"></p><p>15% 20% </p><p>So, the ratio of boys to girls = 15/20 = 3/4 </p><p>Hence, the total number of boys = 14700 * 3/(3 + 4) = 6300</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=310 height=106 id=\"Picture 6\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27135/image003.png\"></p><p>15% 20% </p><p>So, the ratio of boys to girls = 15/20 = 3/4 </p><p>Hence, the total number of boys = 14700 * 3/(3 + 4) = 6300</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixture & Alligation"}, {"q_en": "<p>A runs 22.5% faster than B and can allow B a lead of 36 meters to end a race in a dead heat. What is the length of the race? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>A, B &#2360;&#2375; 22.5% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2340;&#2375;&#2332; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2379; 36 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2340; &#2342;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; &#2354;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;? </p>", "options_en": ["144 meters", "196 meters", "184 meters", "158 meters"], "options_hi": ["144 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "196 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "184 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "158 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the speed of B be '100'</p><p>The speed of A = 100 * 22.5/100 = 122.5</p><p>The ratio of speed of A to B = 122.5/100 = 49:40</p><p>Therefore, the ratio of distance covered by them will also be 49: 40</p><p>49 unit -  40 unit = 36 meters</p><p>9 unit= 36 meters</p><p>1 unit= 4 meters</p><p>49 unit = 196 meters</p><p>Hence, the length of the race = 196 meters</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the speed of B be '100'</p><p>The speed of A = 100 * 22.5/100 = 122.5</p><p>The ratio of speed of A to B = 122.5/100 = 49:40</p><p>Therefore, the ratio of distance covered by them will also be 49: 40</p><p>49 unit -  40 unit = 36 meters</p><p>9 unit= 36 meters</p><p>1 unit= 4 meters</p><p>49 unit = 196 meters</p><p>Hence, the length of the race = 196 meters</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of age of X after 7 years and the age of Y after 9 years is 5:7 respectively and the ratio of present age of X and Y is 2:3 respectively. Find the age of X after 10 years.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>7 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; X &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2324;&#2352; 9 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; Y &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 5:7 &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; X &#2324;&#2352; Y &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 2:3 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 10 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; X &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351;&#2369; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["15 years", "25 years", "18 years", "22 years"], "options_hi": ["15 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "25 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "18 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;", "22 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let present age of X and Y are '2m' years and '3m' years respectively.</p><p>According to the question-</p><p>(2m + 7)/(3m + 9) = 5/7</p><p>14m + 49 = 15m + 45</p><p>m = 4</p><p>The age of X after 10 years = 2*4 + 10 = 18 years</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let present age of X and Y are '2m' years and '3m' years respectively.</p><p>According to the question-</p><p>(2m + 7)/(3m + 9) = 5/7</p><p>14m + 49 = 15m + 45</p><p>m = 4</p><p>The age of X after 10 years = 2*4 + 10 = 18 years</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>If x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> = 193 and xy = 84, then find the value of x<sup>3</sup>  -  y<sup>3</sup>.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> = 193 &#2324;&#2352; xy = 84 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; x<sup>3</sup> - y<sup>3 </sup>&#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1385", "1650", "1260", "1184"], "options_hi": ["1385", "1650", "1260", "1184"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> = 193 and xy = 84</p><p>(x  -  y)<sup>2</sup> = x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup>  -  2xy = 193  -  2*84 = 25</p><p>x  -  y = 5</p><p>x<sup>3</sup>  -  y<sup>3</sup> = (x  -  y)<sup>3</sup> + 3xy(x - y)</p><p>= (5)<sup>3</sup> + 3*84*(5)</p><p>= 5*(25 + 252)</p><p>= 1385</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> = 193 and xy = 84</p><p>(x  -  y)<sup>2</sup> = x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup>  -  2xy = 193  -  2*84 = 25</p><p>x  -  y = 5</p><p>x<sup>3</sup>  -  y<sup>3</sup> = (x  -  y)<sup>3</sup> + 3xy(x - y)</p><p>= (5)<sup>3</sup> + 3*84*(5)</p><p>= 5*(25 + 252)</p><p>= 1385</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>If a certain sum of money at simple interest amounts to Rs.4790 in 1.5 years and to Rs.5080 in 4.5 years, then what is the principal?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; 1.5 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2369;.4790 &#2324;&#2352; 4.5 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2369;.5080 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2343;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.4215", "Rs.4825", "Rs.4645", "Rs.4245"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;.4215", "&#2352;&#2369;.4825", "&#2352;&#2369;.4645", "&#2352;&#2369;.4245"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Simple interest of 3 years = Rs.5080  -  4790 = Rs.290</p><p>Simple interest of 1.5 years = 290 * 1.5/3 = Rs.145</p><p>Principal = Amount  -  Simple interest</p><p>= 4790  -  145 = Rs.4645</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Simple interest of 3 years = Rs.5080  -  4790 = Rs.290</p><p>Simple interest of 1.5 years = 290 * 1.5/3 = Rs.145</p><p>Principal = Amount  -  Simple interest</p><p>= 4790  -  145 = Rs.4645</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the number of zeroes in the product <img width=200 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27304/image001.png\">.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2347;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2370;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; <img width=200 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27304/image001.png\">.</p>", "options_en": ["21", "22", "25", "23"], "options_hi": ["21", "22", "25", "23"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=200 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27304/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=255 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27304/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=205 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27304/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=151 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27304/image004.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=200 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27304/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=255 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27304/image002.png\"></p><p><img width=205 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27304/image003.png\"></p><p><img width=151 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27304/image004.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Simplify:</p><p><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">(7mn)<sup>2</sup>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2352;&#2354;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;:</p><p><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">(7mn)<sup>2</sup>", "options_en": ["7", "14", "49", "21"], "options_hi": ["7", "14", "49", "21"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=205 height=52 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23984/image021.png\"></p><p><img width=219 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23984/image022.png\"></p><p><img width=221 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23984/image023.png\"></p><p><img width=33 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23984/image024.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=205 height=52 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23984/image021.png\"></p><p><img width=219 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23984/image022.png\"></p><p><img width=221 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23984/image023.png\"></p><p><img width=33 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23984/image024.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>A long ladder is leaning against a wall, forming an angle &#952; with the ground. It is given that cosec &#952; = 85/84. Additionally, the foot of the ladder is positioned 10.4 meters away from the base of the wall. Based on this information, determine the height at which the top of the ladder touches the wall.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2360;&#2368;&#2338;&#2364;&#2368; &#2342;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2361;&#2366;&#2352;&#2375; &#2335;&#2367;&#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2379; &#2332;&#2364;&#2350;&#2368;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#952; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2361; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; cosec &#952; = 85/84 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;, &#2360;&#2368;&#2338;&#2364;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2376;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 10.4 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352;, &#2357;&#2361; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2368;&#2338;&#2364;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2342;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2331;&#2370;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["68 m", "72 m", "74.6 m", "67.2 m"], "options_hi": ["68 &#2350;&#2368;", "72 &#2350;&#2368;", "74.6 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;", "67.2 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=205 height=98 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27478/image008.png\"></p><p>AB = Perpendicular, BC = Base, AC = Hypotenuse</p><p>sin &#952; = 1/cosec &#952;</p><p>sin &#952; = 84/85 = AB/AC</p><p>cos<sup>2</sup>&#952; = 1  -  sin<sup>2</sup> &#952;</p><p>cos<sup>2</sup>&#952; = 1  -  (84/85)<sup>2</sup></p><p>cos<sup>2</sup>&#952; = 169/7225 = 13/85 = BC/AC</p><p>13/85 = 10.4/AC</p><p>AC = 68 m</p><p>sin 84/85 = AB/AC</p><p>84/85 = AB/68</p><p>AB = 67.2 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=205 height=98 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27478/image008.png\"></p><p>AB = Perpendicular, BC = Base, AC = Hypotenuse</p><p>sin &#952; = 1/cosec &#952;</p><p>sin &#952; = 84/85 = AB/AC</p><p>cos<sup>2</sup>&#952; = 1  -  sin<sup>2</sup> &#952;</p><p>cos<sup>2</sup>&#952; = 1  -  (84/85)<sup>2</sup></p><p>cos<sup>2</sup>&#952; = 169/7225 = 13/85 = BC/AC</p><p>13/85 = 10.4/AC</p><p>AC = 68 m</p><p>sin 84/85 = AB/AC</p><p>84/85 = AB/68</p><p>AB = 67.2 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Height & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Three partners P, Q and R invest Rs.1000, Rs.1200 and Rs.1500, respectively in a business. What should be the share of Q if the total profit is Rs.666?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2375;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; P, Q &#2324;&#2352; R &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#2352;&#2369;.1000 , &#2352;&#2369;.1200 &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2369;.1500 &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2352;&#2369;.666 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; Q &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;&#2366;&#2306;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.216", "Rs.275", "Rs.252", "Rs.284"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;.216", "&#2352;&#2369;.275", "&#2352;&#2369;.252", "&#2352;&#2369;.284"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Since their investment period is same which means ratio of their profit will be equal to the ratio of their investment.</p><p>Ratio of profit share of P, Q, and R = 1000: 1200: 1500 = 10: 12: 15 = 10x: 12x: 15x</p><p>Total profit = 10x + 12x + 15x = 37x = 666</p><p>x = 18</p><p>Profit share of Q = 12x = &#8377;216</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Since their investment period is same which means ratio of their profit will be equal to the ratio of their investment.</p><p>Ratio of profit share of P, Q, and R = 1000: 1200: 1500 = 10: 12: 15 = 10x: 12x: 15x</p><p>Total profit = 10x + 12x + 15x = 37x = 666</p><p>x = 18</p><p>Profit share of Q = 12x = &#8377;216</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<div>&nbsp;Pipe A alone can fill a tank in 1 hour 4 minutes, while pipe B alone can empty the tank in 2(&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">10", "q_hi": "<p>&#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; 1 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; 4 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; B &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; 2(10/11) &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; 48 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2352;&#2361;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["31.5%", "52.5%", "46.5%", "68.5%"], "options_hi": ["31.5%", "52.5%", "46.5%", "68.5%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Pipe A can fill a tank in 1 hour 4 minutes = 64 minutes</p><p>And pipe B can empty the tank in 2(10/11) hours = 32/11 * 60 = 1920/11</p><p>Part of tank will be filled in 1 minute when both pipes are opened = 1/64  -  11/1920 = 19/1920</p><p>So, in 48 minutes part of tank filled = 48 * 19/1920 = 19/40</p><p>Hence, remaining part = 1  -  19/40 = 21/40 part</p><p>Remaining percentage of the tank = 21/40 * 100 = 52.5%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Pipe A can fill a tank in 1 hour 4 minutes = 64 minutes</p><p>And pipe B can empty the tank in 2(10/11) hours = 32/11 * 60 = 1920/11</p><p>Part of tank will be filled in 1 minute when both pipes are opened = 1/64  -  11/1920 = 19/1920</p><p>So, in 48 minutes part of tank filled = 48 * 19/1920 = 19/40</p><p>Hence, remaining part = 1  -  19/40 = 21/40 part</p><p>Remaining percentage of the tank = 21/40 * 100 = 52.5%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the range of the following data:</p><p>32, 30, 70, 53, 43, 76, 108, 30, 24, 54, 48, 42, 65, 97, 109, 22, 75, 61, 50, 52</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2337;&#2375;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2368;&#2350;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;:</p><p>32, 30, 70, 53, 43, 76, 108, 30, 24, 54, 48, 42, 65, 97, 109, 22, 75, 61, 50, 52</p>", "options_en": ["87", "85", "82", "95"], "options_hi": ["87", "85", "82", "95"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Minimum term = 22</p><p>Maximum term = 109</p><p>Range = maximum  -  minimum = 109  -  22 = 87</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Minimum term = 22</p><p>Maximum term = 109</p><p>Range = maximum  -  minimum = 109  -  22 = 87</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Statistics"}, {"q_en": "<p>If n(A &#8745; B)' = 7, then find the number of elements in A' <img width=15 height=12 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27664/image001.png\"> B'.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; n(A &#8745; B)' = 7 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; A' <img width=15 height=12 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27664/image001.png\"> B' &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["14", "49", "7", "Cannot be determined"], "options_hi": ["14", "49", "7", "&#2340;&#2351; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Using the formula of De Morgan's Law:</p><p>(A &#8745; B)' = A' <img width=15 height=12 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27664/image001.png\"> B'</p><p>Therefore, number of elements in A' <img width=15 height=12 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27664/image001.png\"> B' = 7</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Using the formula of De Morgan's Law:</p><p>(A &#8745; B)' = A' <img width=15 height=12 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27664/image001.png\"> B'</p><p>Therefore, number of elements in A' <img width=15 height=12 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27664/image001.png\"> B' = 7</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}]}